  "caption": "Residual bias and error scale across X families.",
  "reading_guide": "The left heat strip maps signed mean residual Vhat-V to blue-white-amber, centred at zero; signed values preserve the encoding in grayscale. Each right-panel row is explicitly labelled with its X family. Solid green bars encode RMSE; hatched pink bars encode empirical absolute-residual q95. Paired bars start from the same zero on the original-V scale and carry their values at the ends. The two summaries are not additive and are not stacked. Each family contains 1,608 external OOF predictions from frozen H-soft. N3 has the largest RMSE (6.6515) and absolute-error q95 (13.8694). These are empirical error summaries, not calibrated prediction intervals.",
